 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl shadow-sm bg-[color:var(--nv-accent-2-soft-bg)] text-[color:var(--nv-accent-2-soft-fg)]\"></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--nv-muted)]\">Common Questions</p><h2 id=\"faq-heading\" class=\"text-xl font-bold leading-tight text-[color:var(--nv-ink)] sm:text-2xl\">Frequently Asked Questions about Sebastian</h2><p class=\"mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--nv-muted)]\">Common questions about the meaning and origin of Sebastian.</p></div></div><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-3\"><details class=\"group rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--nv-border)] bg-[color:var(--nv-surface)] transition hover:border-[color:var(--nv-accent-2)]/30 hover:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 text-sm font-semibold text-[color:var(--nv-ink)] transition-colors hover:text-[color:var(--nv-accent-2)]\"><span class=\"flex-1\">What does Sebastian mean?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-[color:var(--nv-muted)] transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--nv-muted)]\">Sebastian is a Latin name derived from Sebastianus, meaning &#x27;revered, venerable&#x27;.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--nv-border)] bg-[color:var(--nv-surface)] transition hover:border-[color:var(--nv-accent-2)]/30 hover:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 text-sm font-semibold text-[color:var(--nv-ink)] transition-colors hover:text-[color:var(--nv-accent-2)]\"><span class=\"flex-1\">Is Sebastian a Christianity name?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-[color:var(--nv-muted)] transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--nv-muted)]\">Yes, Sebastian has been used throughout history as a name for several saints and martyrs in Christian tradition.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--nv-border)] bg-[color:var(--nv-surface)] transition hover:border-[color:var(--nv-accent-2)]/30 hover:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 text-sm font-semibold text-[color:var(--nv-ink)] transition-colors hover:text-[color:var(--nv-accent-2)]\"><span class=\"flex-1\">How to pronounce Sebastian?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-[color:var(--nv-muted)] transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--nv-muted)]\">Seb-astian</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--nv-border)] bg-[color:var(--nv-surface)] transition hover:border-[color:var(--nv-accent-2)]/30 hover:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 text-sm font-semibold text-[color:var(--nv-ink)] transition-colors hover:text-[color:var(--nv-accent-2)]\"><span class=\"flex-1\">Is Sebastian popular today?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-[color:var(--nv-muted)] transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--nv-muted)]\">Yes, Sebastian continues to be a popular name today, often associated with strength, devotion, and reverence.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--nv-border)] bg-[color:var(--nv-surface)] transition hover:border-[color:var(--nv-accent-2)]/30 hover:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 text-sm font-semibold text-[color:var(--nv-ink)] transition-colors hover:text-[color:var(--nv-accent-2)]\"><span class=\"flex-1\">What is the origin of Sebastian?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-[color:var(--nv-muted)] transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--nv-muted)]\">Sebastian is a Latin name derived from Sebastianus, meaning &#x27;revered, venerable&#x27;.</div></details></div></section></div></div></main><!--$--><!--/$--></div></div><footer class=\"border-t border-nv-border bg-nv-surface\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><div class=\"grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.3fr_1fr_1fr_1fr]\"><div><a class=\"flex items-center gap-3\" href=\"/\"><div class=\"grid h-11 w-11 place-items-center rounded-lg bg